1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,528
They charged my mother three hundred dollars yesterday just for crying too loudly at her own brother's funeral.

2
00:00:06,828 --> 00:00:14,460
Every single sound in this city has a price tag attached by the relentless, invisible hands of the municipal board.

3
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:21,432
I whispered a secret to my best friend, and my bank account drained before the final syllable left my lips.

4
00:00:21,732 --> 00:00:27,348
We live in a world where holding your breath is cheaper than daring to speak your mind out loud.

5
00:00:27,648 --> 00:00:34,728
Today my balance hit zero, meaning I officially lost the legal right to utter another single word in public.

6
00:00:35,028 --> 00:00:42,516
That is when I noticed the sleek fiber-optic cables running directly from the city's audio sensors into corporate vaults.

7
00:00:42,816 --> 00:00:51,840
They are not just taxing our conversations. They are recording, packaging, and selling our deepest memories back to tourists.

8
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:58,620
My stolen words are sitting on a luxury shelf right now, waiting for a stranger to buy my laughter.

9
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:07,392
I take a deep breath, open my mouth wide, and scream the loudest, most expensive rebellion this city has ever heard.

10
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:13,932
If every word you utter builds a cage, how long until you choose to stay locked inside forever?
